      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf will form stable nanoscale oxide or intermetallic precipitates in TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512535::web::030::5_summary"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf segregation or precipitate formation will refine the TiVNbTa microstructure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf-induced segregation or precipitates will impede dislocation motion and grain-boundary migration.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512535::web::030::5_summary",
        "PMC9586648::web::024::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding Hf will increase both yield strength and compressive strength at 1273 K by approximately 50% relative to baseline TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-modified alloy will retain ductility in the 30–40% range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512535::web::030::5_summary"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-modified alloy will retain a single-phase BCC structure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted benefit applies around 1273 K and at strains up to 40%.",
